### Cancel pending glide and inertia when Ctrl is held

**Severity:** `medium`

With Smooth scroll enabled, Ctrl held after the last wheel tick does not stop queued glide or inertia: the existing Ctrl check runs only on another non-injected wheel event. Check the key before stepping the timer's state and cancel both axes, so pending deltas are not emitted while Ctrl bypass is active.

```suggestion
                    std::scoped_lock lock(g_momentumMutex);
                    if (g_injectorIgnoreWithCtrl && (GetAsyncKeyState(VK_CONTROL) & 0x8000))
                    {
                        g_verticalMomentum.Cancel();
                        g_horizontalMomentum.Cancel();
                        g_verticalSmoothing.Reset();
                        g_horizontalSmoothing.Reset();
                    }
```

Apply all three suggestions in this group as one batch; they form one Ctrl-cancellation correction.
